DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260610T150000
UID:69ea47a9bd9a3c316a54df7b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Senior Safety Awareness Month Toronto Fire S
 ervices is hosting a 60 Minute Senior Fire Safety presentation followed 
 by a Q & A.\nTopics to be covered:\nPreventing a fire from happening to yo
 u   Causes of home fires   Placement/Need for smoke & CO alarms\nE
 liminating nuisance alarms   Escape Planning for special need  C
 alling for help (how/when/from where)\nFire safety in High-Rise buildings
LOCATION:Taylor Memorial\, Meeting room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ea47a9bd9a3c316a54df7b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Privacy 101
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260504T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260504T150000
UID:69dfb06766c3387a9d06dcb8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested to learn how to maintain your online privac
 y and how to secure your online accounts and devices? If so\, this is the 
 class for you. Come and join us in this introductory session that is fille
 d with hands-on activities and discussion.\nIn this program\, you will:\nL
 earn how to maintain your online privacy through good habits and the secur
 ity of your accounts and devices.\nDevelop a strong password\, and review 
 the best methods for storing your passwords.\nLearn about various online t
 hreats: malware\, phishing\, hacking\, etc.\nGain an understanding of the 
 limitations of these tools and habits.\nThis is a drop-in program\, space 
 is limited
LOCATION:Brentwood\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69dfb06766c3387a9d06dcb8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
