BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Caregiver's journey: meet the author
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260521T153000
UID:69bdd31fbf48d63c596c421e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This presentation presents both the pitfalls and unexpected mo
 ments of joy that is the life of a caregiver. Paula de Ronde explores how
  a dementia diagnosis effects both the patient and more especially the c
 aregiver. As a caregiver for 11 years\, she charts her journey after her h
 usband's dementia diagnosis as detailed in her memoir:\nMy Bert Has Alzhe
 imer's\n.\nRegistration is available and drop-ins are welcome until capaci
 ty is met.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\nFloor 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69bdd31fbf48d63c596c421e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
