UID:69e133c4bd5c392c7644abba@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy watching DVDs in the Library Auditorium. Coffee\, tea an
 d cookies or snacks will be served after the film.\nIngredient lists will 
 be available upon request.\nBuilding England: Before There Were Architects
 \nThis film explores English building traditions from the early Middle Age
 s to the 17th century\, revealing how remarkable structures were created l
 ong before architecture became a profession. The exhibition highlights sit
 es such as Lindisfarne Monastery\, Durham Cathedral\, Fountains Abbey\, an
 d Kentwell Hall—testaments to centuries of craftsmanship and innovation.
  50 minutes.2017
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e133c4bd5c392c7644abba
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
