DESCRIPTION:Join other knitters and crocheters for our knitting and croche
 t circle! Exchange knitting and crochet tips and tricks. Bring your projec
 ts\, troubleshoot patterns\, or work on that piece you have wanted to try.
  All skill levels welcome. Please bring your own supplies.\nDrop-in every 
 Thursday afternoon.
LOCATION:Kennedy/Eglinton\, Meeting Room 2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698f7cbe6724c63d00f29029
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Innovation Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T200000
UID:69aeee6b45f57dfccb19679b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Conversation is the source of innovation!\nJoin TPL Innovation
  Council member\nZahra Ebrahim\nfor a series of lively book discussions ab
 out how we can build a better world by getting better at talking with eac
 h other.\nAt our June meeting\, we'll discuss the final chapters of\nTalk\
 n: The Science of Conversation and the Art of Being Ourselves\, by Alison 
 Wood Brooks. Learn about:\nLevity - how to let humour make your conversati
 ons better\nKindness - how small changes in what you say can increase war
 mth in conversation and improve your relationships\, at work and in life.\
 nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is 
 collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, s
 ections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for e
 vent and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about h
 ow the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staf
 f at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M
 4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Bloor/Gladstone\, Program room\, lower level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69aeee6b45f57dfccb19679b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Connecting the Dots(?) Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260514T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260514T160000
UID:698e5555707481383709ba64@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wondered why people believe in conspiracies?\nIn
  this book club\, we will be reading books that explore the social conditi
 ons that make people prone to extreme belief.\nThurs. Feb. 12\, 2:00-4:00p
 m\nA Lot of People Are Saying\nby Russell Muirhead\, Nancy Rosenblum\nThur
 s. Mar. 12\, 2:00-4:00pm\nConspiracy\nby Michael Shermer\nThurs. Apr 9\, 2
 :00-4:00pm\nTrust the Plan\nby Will Sommer\nThurs. May 14\, 2:00-4:00pm\nC
 atch and Kill\nby Ronan Farrow **BOOK CHANGE**\nThurs. Jun. 11\, 2:00-4:00
 pm\nEscaping the Rabbit Hole\nby Mick West
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Founder's Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698e5555707481383709ba64
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
