BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Word Basics
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260512T200000
UID:69e249178ddc1caf5f1d86d4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Word Basics 1: Write a Letter (March 9)\nAn introductory class
  on Microsoft Word for absolute beginners.\nIn this class\, you will:\nUnd
 erstand how to use Word’s Tabs\, Groups\, and Commands\nCreate\, save\, 
 print and delete Word documents\nPractice basic text formatting and style 
 features\nUpon completion of this class\, you will be able to use Microsof
 t Word at a basic level.\nPrerequisites: Basic keyboarding and mouse skill
 s required.\nFormat: Hands-on with demonstrations\nWord Basics 2: Basic Re
 sumes with Word (March 16)\nPractice your Microsoft Word skills while crea
 ting a simple resume.\nIn this class\, you will:\nFormat a simple resume\n
 Practice advanced formatting using Ruler Tools and Format Painter\nUse Gra
 mmar and Spell check tools\nPractice using Word’s built-in resume templa
 tes\nSave documents in other formats such as PDF\nUpon completion of this 
 class\, you will be able to create an organized simple resume and access r
 esume templates with additional style options.\nPrerequisites: Word Basics
  1 or equivalent skills. Keyboarding and mouse skills are required.\nForma
 t: Hands-on with demonstrations\nWord Basics 3: Formatting Reports and Lon
 g Documents (March 23)\nPractice your Microsoft Word skills when working w
 ith long documents.\nIn this class\, you will:\nUse Styles to effectively 
 format\, structure and navigate your document\nCreate a Table of Contents\
 nUse Page and Section breaks\nInsert Page Numbers and Footnotes\nInsert We
 b and document links\nLearn about Microsoft Word's Accessibility features\
 nUpon completion of this class\, you will be able to format long documents
 \, such as books\, reports\, and essays.\nPrerequisites: Word Basics 1 & 2
 \, or equivalent skills. Keyboarding and mouse skills are required.\nForma
 t: Hands-on with demonstrations\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe perso
 nal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library un
 der the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inf
 ormation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery a
 nd evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information ca
 n be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\,
  789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:York Woods\, ELC
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e249178ddc1caf5f1d86d4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
