DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260509T150000
UID:69ac4c946583d22e3c0e3e1e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Seniors E-Connect is an intergenerational program that matche
 s older adults with a teen volunteer to provide tech help\, under the guid
 ance of library staff. Learn the basics of using computers\, tablets\, and
  smartphones such as internet browsing\, eBooks\, streaming video\, and us
 ing apps\n.\nGet one-on-one support in a welcoming and friendly environmen
 t.\nDrop-ins welcome until capacity is reached.\nInformation Collection No
 tice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto P
 ublic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, an
 d 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrat
 ion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles you
 r information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\
 , 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, eLearning lab\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ac4c946583d22e3c0e3e1e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Romance Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260507T200000
UID:69d98f88491b809c6f26991f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to the Romance Book Club\, where love stories take cen
 ter stage and every page promises a new adventure of the heart. Whether yo
 u're into slow burns\, second chances\, or enemies-to-lovers\, there's som
 ething here for every kind of romantic. Come read\, swoon\, and share your
  favorite moments with fellow book lovers.\nThe Romance Book Club title fo
 r Thursday May 7 is\nThe Book Tour\nby Emily Ohanjanians.\nPlease note th
 at this book club is for individuals 18+.\nLimited copies will be availabl
 e in branch for pick up.\nDrop in\, no registration required.
LOCATION:Brentwood\, Community Room\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d98f88491b809c6f26991f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film Screening: Nechako: It Will Be a Big River Again
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260609T200000
UID:6995eb2c81b67dfe32a72274@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:National Indigenous Heritage Month film screening\n.\nAfter se
 ven decades of resistances\, two Indigenous Nations reach a turning point 
 in their historic legal fight to reclaim the Nechako River and the way of 
 life it once sustained. This film is a powerful chronicle of resistance an
 d renewal- a call to action reminder us that survival must serve everyone\
 , and that the health of our lands and waters is inseparable from our own\
 nThis film is provided by the National Film Board of Canada.\nInformation 
 Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by 
 the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)
 \, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and prog
 ram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the librar
 y handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerl
 ine@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Pleasant\, Basement program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6995eb2c81b67dfe32a72274
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
