BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Supporting Our Local Pollinators in Small Spaces
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260610T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260610T140000
UID:69dd2348491b809c6f271e01@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Pollinators need a supply of nectar throughout the growing sea
 son\, so if you are planting up pots for your garden or balcony\, why not 
 choose plants that will attract birds\, bees\, and butterflies?\nThis demo
 nstration\, led by a Toronto Master Gardener\, will start with how to choo
 se soil\, plants\, and containers\, and how to arrange them to maximize th
 eir positive impact on the environment.\nAt the end of the demonstration\,
  materials will be shared with participants\, while supplies last.\nThis p
 rogram is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by
  Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.
