DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260513T153000
UID:69dd523fb6c4ac1fedcc20fd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Computers for Beginners is a 6-week course designed to build y
 our confidence by introducing new skills slowly in a small\, supportive co
 mmunity. At the end of the course\, you may not know everything about the 
 internet\, but you will have a solid foundation of new skills and the conf
 idence to continue learning.\nIs This Course Right for You?\nFor seniors a
 nd beginners\; those with very limited or no computer experience\n6 weeks\
 n: with 1 class per week\nWhat Will You Learn?\nBasic tools such as the mo
 use and the keyboard\nHow to search online for information\, services and 
 entertainment\nHow to use email to keep in touch with family and friends\n
 Week 1:\nUse the Mouse (May 6)\nWeek 2:\nUse the Keyboard (May 13)\nA clas
 s on basic keyboard functions for absolute beginners with little or no com
 puter experience.\nIn this second session you will:\nFamiliarize yourself 
 through practice with the most essential keyboard functions (alphabet\, nu
 mber and symbol keys)\nPractice proper keyboarding posture\nUpon completio
 n of this class students will be able to use a keyboard at a beginner leve
 l and know how to go online for additional practice.\nPrerequisites: Compu
 ter for Beginners 1 or basic mouse skills\nWeek 3:\nUse Windows (May 20)\n
 Week 4:\nUse the Internet (May 27)\nWeek 5:\nUse Google/Google Maps (June 
 3)\nWeek 6:\nUse Gmail (June 10)\nPlease read the following information ca
 refully:\nTo register for the\nWeek 1: Use the Mouse\nyou will need to eit
 her register\nin person at the Bloor/Gladstone Library\n\, or call us at\n
 416-393-7674\n. This first class is offline registration because not every
 one knows how to use the computer mouse right away. When you are registeri
 ng online\, you will be registered for all classes from Week 2 - Week 6.\n
 Registration is required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal in
 formation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under th
 e Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informati
 on will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and eva
 luation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be d
 irected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Y
 onge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
